# ==================== RiseOS Environment Variables ====================

# ─── OPTION 1: Local SQLite (default — works out of the box) ───
# No Supabase needed. The app runs with a local SQLite database.
DATABASE_URL=file:./db/riseos.db

# ─── OPTION 2: Supabase (for production / multi-user) ───
# Uncomment these and comment out the DATABASE_URL above.
# Then restore the original src/lib/supabase.ts from the git history
# (the version that uses @supabase/supabase-js directly).
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://xxxxx.supabase.co
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# ─── Optional: Admin email (for admin panel access) ───
# ADMIN_EMAIL=your-email@example.com

# ─── Optional: AI Coach (ZhipuAI / BigModel) ───
# BIGMODEL_API_KEY=your-api-key

# ─── Optional: Dev API keys (comma-separated, bypasses Supabase auth) ───
# RISE_ALLOWED_API_KEYS=rise_xxxxx

# ==================== Notes ====================
# 1. Default mode: local SQLite (no external services needed)
# 2. For Supabase: create a project at https://supabase.com,
#    run supabase/migrations/004_full_fix.sql in the SQL Editor,
#    then set the 3 Supabase env vars above.
# 3. After clone: bun install && bun run dev
